DAY 23 — DISK I/O & PERFORMANCE BASICS
Commands Reference Sheet
Machine: Kali Linux | User: raven
==========================================

--- CHECKING I/O WAIT VIA TOP (recap, new focus) ---
top                                # watch the "wa" value in %Cpu(s) line
                                    # high wa% = CPU waiting on disk, not actually idle

--- IOSTAT (detailed per-disk statistics) ---
sudo apt install sysstat            # install (provides iostat)
iostat                                # one-time snapshot
iostat -x 1                           # extended stats, refresh every 1 second
iostat -x 1 5                          # extended stats, every 1 second, 5 times total
                                        # %util close to 100 = disk is maxed out

--- IOTOP (like top, but for disk I/O per-process) ---
sudo apt install iotop               # install
sudo iotop                            # run (needs root) — shows read/write per process
                                       # q = quit

--- ROUGH DISK SPEED TEST (with dd) ---
dd if=/dev/zero of=testfile bs=1M count=100    # write a 100MB test file, shows speed
rm testfile                                     # ALWAYS clean up the test file after

--- COMBINING WITH DAY 10 (disk usage + performance together) ---
df -h              # how FULL is the disk (Day 10 recap)
iostat -x 1 3       # how BUSY is the disk right now

